b/id #edb/ref 17592186159281}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "94d74135-f328-5641-b2bb-0bbd125b85a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "v_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159279} :answer-field/id #uuid "d30b56ee-52cf-5e42-ab2b-2bbf82995677" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186159276}] :question/id #uuid "14414eae-18ed-5455-a3d4-1f9724606970" :question/math-academy-id "q-139421" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/3131/Source/Images/q-139421.png)\n\nA $2 \\cdot 2$ matrix $A$ maps the unit circle ${x \\mid ‖x‖ = 1}$ from $R^{2}$ onto an ellipse in $R^{2}$. The corresponding ellipse and its principal axes are depicted in the diagram above. Given that $v_{1}$ and $v_{2}$ are unit eigenvectors of $A^{T}A$, which of the following is an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $25$ of $A^{T}A$?"}]}
